--- body ---
## Context
0180 corrects the external attributions that are wrong today. This ticket
stops the class returning, which a per-PR review cannot do: the defect is a
sentence that reads plausibly and is wrong about a repository nobody opens
during review.

The guard: a claim in the specification chain about Zotero, #6012 or zoteus
must carry the coordinate that settles it — a file, a line, and the SHA it
was read at. A claim with no coordinate is a claim nobody can re-check, and
this repo has now produced four of them.

Related but distinct: ticket 0161 guards that prose quoting **our own**
measurements is covered by the figure guard. This one guards claims about
**someone else's** code. Same discipline, different corpus, and neither
subsumes the other — 0161 would pass a document full of uncited assertions
about upstream, and this one would pass a document with a wrong number of
our own.

## Actions
1. Decide the coordinate form and where it lives. Inline is noisy in prose;
   a reference block at the foot of each document, keyed from the sentence,
   is likely better. Weigh it — do not default to inline.
2. Write the check. It must find attribution sentences by more than the
   "verbatim / adopted / #6012's" vocabulary that seeded 0180, because a
   claim can assert platform behaviour in plain words.
3. Decide the failure mode. A hard fail on any uncited attribution will be
   fought and then disabled; a report that lists uncited claims and fails
   only on a *new* one is the ratchet shape this repo already uses
   elsewhere.
4. Add a staleness dimension: #6012 is an open draft. A coordinate read at a
   SHA that upstream has moved past is a claim to re-check, not a claim to
   trust. `make upstream-status` already detects movement.

## Test
The guard must fail against the tree as it stood on 2026-08-29 before 0180 —
four uncited-or-wrong attributions were live then, so that is the positive
control. A guard that has never been red has not been shown to be able to go
red, and this repo has met that failure twice this session.

## Verification
- [ ] The check fails on the pre-0180 tree and passes after it
- [ ] A newly added uncited attribution turns it red
- [ ] It does not fire on prose that makes no external claim

## Invariants
- The guard reports; it does not edit prose.
- It must not duplicate 0161's figure-guard coverage; if the two overlap,
  say which owns what rather than letting both check the same line.
- No new dependency for a check this small.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The guard exists, with its positive control demonstrated
- [ ] Its relationship to 0161 is stated, not left implicit
- [ ] `make check` runs it and passes
